{
  "$schema": "../../../../docs/catalog/schema/package.schema.json",
  "id": "Lyo.Algorithms.Api",
  "name": "Lyo.Algorithms.Api",
  "area": "Apps",
  "tagline": "HTTP mapping for the Lyo algorithm catalog (`BuildAlgorithmsGroup`).",
  "description": "Maps catalog list, get, revision append, revert, label, delete, and preview routes. Writes go through `IAlgorithmCatalog` so syntax and startup-key checks still run. Reads return the store's `*Res` types with no second mapping. `Kind` is `AlgorithmKind`. Revert takes `AlgorithmRevertReq`. `DELETE Algorithms/{key}` removes the definition, its revisions, and its labels. `POST Algorithms/preview` runs an unsaved draft and does not append a revision. Catalog execute stays in-process. Register with `AddAlgorithmsApiFromConfiguration` (section `PostgresAlgorithms`), then call `BuildAlgorithmsGroup`.",
  "features": [
    "`BuildAlgorithmsGroup` maps GET /Algorithms, GET by key, revisions, revert, labels, DELETE by key, and POST /Algorithms/preview.",
    "`POST Algorithms/preview` converts the context JSON with the revision type binding and returns `value`, the result alias, and the step breakdown.",
    "POST revisions and revert, and PUT labels, return `AlgorithmDefinitionRes` or `AlgorithmLabelRes`. Failed catalog results are 400.",
    "`AddAlgorithmsApiFromConfiguration` registers the Postgres store and `AddAlgorithms`."
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "title": "Map the Algorithms API",
      "language": "csharp",
      "code": "services.AddAlgorithmsApiFromConfiguration(configuration);\nvar app = builder.Build();\napp.BuildAlgorithmsGroup();"
    }
  ],
